      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Crack First Category tempate:  ( rippilng, uber ) -> we do have single file write all code in it. \n\nTime 45 mins.\n\n\n\n1. Requirements ( given , interview will get this requirements. ): \n    -> requirements will be given like the dsa problem, but with flavor of real world. E.g rippling. \n\n\n2. Understand the requirements: -> 5-10 mins. atmax. \n\n\n\n-> ask for interviewer about the expecation -> solved, design pattern etc. \n\n3. Coding:  -> remaining 35-40mins. \n    -> no dao layer\n    -> no service layer\n    -> no controller layer\n    -> no multiple files. \n    ....................................\n    -> only one file , write all code in it. \n\nUseful things: \n    -> problem solving , dsa in that language. \n    -> oops -> know how to create class and operate on it\n        instead of normal data type on STL ( in c++ ) , need to have\n        idea how to work making custom data type and how to operate\n        STL on them. \n\n    -> class -> attributes, constructor, destructor, methods etc.  -> imp. \n    -> interfaces and abstract class -> imp. \n    -> inheritance as well. \n    -> normal class with STL on them(like key of map, sorting etc.), polymorphism\n        -> how to function override. \n        -> few operation loading.\n        -> how to do overriding. \n    -> SOLID, OOPS\n\n    -> usually not much design patten require here, except interfaces, inheritance, polymorphism. \n        but some time can use differnt design pattern like stratedy etc. \n\n    -> these problme usually have follow up. So make the class or structure\n        the class in extendable manner\n\n\n  ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Crack First Category tempate:  ( rippilng, uber ) -> we do have single file write all code in it. \n\nTime 45 mins.\n\n\n\n1. Requirements ( given , interview will get this requirements. ): \n    -> requirements will be given like the dsa problem, but with flavor of real world. E.g rippling. \n\n\n2. Understand the requirements: -> 5-10 mins. atmax. \n\n\n\n-> ask for interviewer about the expecation -> solved, design pattern etc. \n\n3. Coding:  -> remaining 35-40mins. \n    -> no dao layer\n    -> no service layer\n    -> no controller layer\n    -> no multiple files. \n    ....................................\n    -> only one file , write all code in it. \n\nUseful things: \n    -> problem solving , dsa in that language. \n    -> oops -> know how to create class and operate on it\n        instead of normal data type on STL ( in c++ ) , need to have\n        idea how to work making custom data type and how to operate\n        STL on them. \n\n    -> class -> attributes, constructor, destructor, methods etc.  -> imp. \n    -> interfaces and abstract class -> imp. \n    -> inheritance as well. \n    -> normal class with STL on them(like key of map, sorting etc.), polymorphism\n        -> how to function override. \n        -> few operation loading.\n        -> how to do overriding. \n    -> SOLID, OOPS\n\n    -> usually not much design patten require here, except interfaces, inheritance, polymorphism. \n        but some time can use differnt design pattern like stratedy etc. \n\n    -> these problme usually have follow up. So make the class or structure\n        the class in extendable manner\n\n\n  ",
